    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23287" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάκρυ</span></b> , τό, used by
		Poets metri gr. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάκρυον</span> in sg.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάκρυ</span> and dat. pl. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάκρυσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.570
				</span></i>
			, etc.: dat. pl. sts. in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.75
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				30.32
			</span></i>, <i>Eu/.Luc.</i><i><span class="en">
				7.38
			</span></i>: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάκρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>An.Ox.</u>
					1.121
				</span></i>
			 (cj. Bgk. in <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				122.3
			</span></i>, cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάκρυον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2
				</span></i>
			):—<i>tear,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.266
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.114
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				638
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ὅ γε δ. χέων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.24
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> generally,
				<i>drop,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιβάνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. πεύκινον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					1200
				</span></i>
			. (Cf.Lat. <i>lacruma,</i> Goth. <i>tagr,</i> O<i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>
			<i>tear.</i>)</div>
